+      <p className="mb-4">You can request deletion from Settings in the app or website. Sign in to the account you want to delete, open Settings, choose Delete account, and confirm your request.</p>
+      <p className="mb-4"><Link className="underline" href="/settings">Open account settings</Link></p>
+      <h2 className="mb-3 mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">If you cannot sign in</h2>
+      <p className="mb-4">Email <a className="underline" href="mailto:support@mydearpartner.in?subject=Account%20deletion%20request">support@mydearpartner.in</a> from your registered email address. Include your registered phone number or member ID so support can identify the account and verify ownership. Never send your password, payment details, identity documents, or one-time codes by email.</p>
+      <h2 className="mb-3 mt-8 text-xl font-semibold">What happens after a request</h2>
+      <p className="mb-4">An in-app request moves your account into a pending deletion state and hides it from other members. The confirmation shows your recovery deadline. The current recovery window is 30 days. After that deadline, the service schedules permanent cleanup of your account, profile, photos and uploaded documents.</p>
+      <p className="mb-4">Limited payment, safety, fraud-prevention or legally required records may be retained. Messages or copies already received by other people may remain. Support can explain what applies to your request and confirm its status. An email request requires ownership verification before account changes are made.</p>
+      <p className="mt-8"><Link className="underline" href="/privacy">Read the privacy policy</Link></p>
+    </main>
+  );
+}
